  "history_of_present_illness": "The 91\u2011year\u2011old female has progressive CKD now stage 4 (onset 2018) and is awaiting kidney transplantation. She has longstanding type 2 diabetes (diagnosed 1988) with microvascular complications (retinopathy, proteinuria, microalbuminuria) and macrovascular disease (ischemic heart disease with prior CABG in 2008). Hypertension, hyperlipidemia, obesity and metabolic syndrome are present. Recent labs show an A1c of 3.1%, suggesting possible overtreatment. Current medication list includes insulin, metformin, hydrochlorothiazide, beta\u2011blocker, clopidogrel, nitroglycerin and multiple simvastatin entries, raising safety concerns (metformin in CKD\u20114, duplicate statins). She reports stress, recent intimate\u2011partner abuse, full\u2011time employment and limited education, all potentially impacting adherence. No recent blood pressure, eGFR, or lipid values are available. Overall picture is high cardiovascular\u2011renal\u2011metabolic risk with gaps in guideline\u2011directed therapy.",
